    "universal_harmonization": "Whether driven by carbamazepine autoinduction and epoxide hydrolase saturation or valproate-induced UGT blockade shunting lamotrigine toward oxidative metabolism, Cytochrome P450-catalyzed aromatic epoxidation is the identical, indispensable forward chemical reaction generating the pathogenic immunogen."
  },
  "locked_final_submission": {
    "primary_answer": "Cytochrome P450–mediated aromatic oxidation / epoxidation (formation of a reactive arene oxide intermediate).",
    "contextual_support": "Upstream inhibition of UDP-glucuronosyltransferase (UGT)–mediated glucuronidation causes parent drug accumulation and shunts metabolism into this oxidative bioactivation pathway."
  }
}

